# Line endings for scripts that must run on Linux/macOS.
#
# Git already stores LF correctly. The problem this file solves is the CHECKOUT
# side: on a Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) every shell script lands in the
# working tree as CRLF. Push one of those to the Deck and bash dies with an
# unreadable "$'\r': command not found". Pinning eol=lf keeps them LF even in a
# Windows working copy. (deck/deck-push.sh also strips CRs on the far side, but
# belt and braces.)
#
# Deliberately NOT setting eol=crlf on *.bat / *.ps1: they already behave, and
# declaring it only churns their stored blobs for no gain.

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
*.desktop   text eol=lf

# Never apply text conversion to these - a stray CRLF pass corrupts them.
*.png       binary
*.exe       binary
*.dll       binary
*.pyc       binary
*.pix       binary
*.vdf       binary
*.svg       -text

# The shipped Windows control map is installed byte for byte and its md5 is printed on the
# quick reference sheet. It has mixed line endings (as the owner's game folder has it), so
# no conversion in either direction.
shared/controls/input.map -text

# Windows batch files: cmd mis-handles labels and goto in LF-only files (TEST-FRAMERATE.bat skipped a menu, 2026-10-03)
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The three promoted presets and the daily driver's launch confs are copied into game folders and compared by
# md5 against the golden copy's PROMOTIONS.md (best-wide 8de71421, best-wide-balanced a2191719, best-120 3c12c8d0,
# dgVoodoo.wide.conf ac0ecdeb, dgVoodoo.16x10.conf 299a6811). The driver's files have mixed line endings
# (best-wide / best-120 LF, best-wide-balanced CRLF, the confs CRLF), so the presets are stored byte for byte
# with no conversion and the confs are pinned CRLF: a checkout is byte-equal whatever core.autocrlf says.
shared/presets/best-wide.psd1           -text
shared/presets/best-wide-balanced.psd1  -text
shared/presets/best-120.psd1            -text
tools/conf/*.conf                       text eol=crlf
dgVoodoo.daily-driver-2026-10-03.conf   text eol=crlf

# The I'76 Mac Kit (tools/mac-kit) is read by bash / awk on a Mac: pins.txt, the env files, the README and the profile
# must stay LF in a Windows working copy too (a CR at a URL's end breaks curl). The launch stubs are Mach-O binaries.
tools/mac-kit/**                text eol=lf
tools/mac-kit/stubs/Sikarugir-* binary

# Windows batch files: CRLF in the working tree always (cmd.exe wants it), LF in the repo like everything else.
*.bat text eol=crlf
